  <section class="tale wrap" aria-labelledby="tale-title">
    <header class="tale-intro">
      <h2 id="tale-title">The same tale, told in your repository.</h2>
      <p>Agents work fast and forget fast. When requirements live in chat history, every new session starts from nothing and no reviewer shares a definition of done. Solomonar gives the work the shape of the old story: one book, a few spells, dragons with distinct jobs, and someone holding the reins.</p>
    </header>
    <ol class="tale-thread">
      <li class="tale-chapter" id="book">
        <div class="tale-text">
          <h3><span class="chapter-number">01</span> The book</h3>
          <p class="tale-folk">The solomonar learned every secret from a single book.</p>
          <p>Your book is the specification: version-controlled files that say what the software must do. The <code>spec</code> skill keeps what a prototype happened to do apart from what you agreed, and leaves the rest as open questions.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="{{ '/docs/framework/#the-book-specifications' | url }}">How specifications work <svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="{{ '/assets/icons.svg#arrow-right' | url }}"></use></svg></a>
        </div>
        <figure class="swatch">
          <figcaption>docs/specs/expenses.md</figcaption>
<pre><code>## Rules

- expenses/R-1 · <b>Agreed</b> · If the amount is not a
  positive number, then the system shall show an error
  and add no expense. · user 2026-10-21
- expenses/R-2 · <i>Observed</i> · When the page reloads,
  the system shall still list a saved expense.

## Open questions

- expenses/Q-1 · Where are expenses stored?
  · needs decision: yes</code></pre>
        </figure>
      </li>
      <li class="tale-chapter" id="spells">
        <div class="tale-text">
          <h3><span class="chapter-number">02</span> The spells</h3>
          <p class="tale-folk">Knowledge became a method, spoken when needed.</p>
          <p>Skills are short procedures your agent loads on demand: try a flow as a clickable prototype, turn it into rules, prepare one task. You call them in plain words from your configured agent session.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="{{ '/docs/use-cases/' | url }}">Prompts for real situations <svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="{{ '/assets/icons.svg#arrow-right' | url }}"></use></svg></a>
        </div>
        <figure class="swatch">
          <figcaption>Your agent session</figcaption>
<pre class="copyable"><code><b>/solomonar</b> Prototype adding a shared expense.
Let me try the empty list, a valid expense,
and an invalid amount. Use fictional data;
do not choose a production stack yet.</code></pre>
        </figure>
      </li>
      <li class="tale-chapter" id="dragon">
        <div class="tale-text">
          <h3><span class="chapter-number">03</span> The dragon</h3>
          <p class="tale-folk">A dragon carried the storm, but never chose its course.</p>
          <p>Agents do the heavy work, each with one job. An implementer builds the change. Separate reviewers check security, correctness, and the spec, and risky changes face a reviewer whose only aim is to break them. No agent approves its own work.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="{{ '/docs/framework/#the-dragons-agents' | url }}">Meet the agents <svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="{{ '/assets/icons.svg#arrow-right' | url }}"></use></svg></a>
        </div>
        <figure class="swatch">
          <figcaption>.claude/agents/</figcaption>
<pre><code>implementer.md            builds one candidate
security-reviewer.md      trust boundaries, secrets
correctness-reviewer.md   rules, edge cases
spec-reviewer.md          scope and contracts
adversarial-reviewer.md   tries to break tier 2</code></pre>
        </figure>
      </li>
      <li class="tale-chapter" id="direction">
        <div class="tale-text">
          <h3><span class="chapter-number">04</span> The direction</h3>
          <p class="tale-folk">Every dragon needs a little direction.</p>
          <p>You hold the reins through one orchestrator session per task, and a CLI that records each step in Git. The orchestrator decides; the CLI checks, and refuses a step the record cannot support.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="{{ '/docs/workflow/' | url }}">Follow a task to merge <svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="{{ '/assets/icons.svg#arrow-right' | url }}"></use></svg></a>
        </div>
        <figure class="swatch">
          <figcaption>Terminal</figcaption>
<pre><code>$ solomonar task move W-001 --as orchestrator-1 \
    --stage implementation
<b>error:</b> task move W-001 rejected (spec_required)
  check: a stage from implementation onward
         needs a recorded spec
  found: implementation without spec
  fix:   pass --spec &lt;worktree-relative path&gt;
nothing was written</code></pre>
        </figure>
      </li>
    </ol>
    <section class="first-stitch" aria-labelledby="first-stitch-title">
      <div class="tale-text">
        <h2 id="first-stitch-title">Start with one stitch.</h2>
        <p>Install the CLI, then run <code>init</code> in your repository. It copies the book, the spells, and the agents into your project and creates the task registry. The CLI never calls a model: your agent runtime does the work, and the CLI keeps the record honest.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button" href="{{ '/docs/getting-started/' | url }}">Get started <svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="{{ '/assets/icons.svg#arrow-right' | url }}"></use></svg></a><a class="text-link" href="{{ '/docs/story/' | url }}">The story behind the name</a></div>
        <p class="development-note"><span class="status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> <span>Available today: <code>init</code>, <code>upgrade</code>, the <code>extension</code> commands with the <code>go</code> and <code>extension-authoring</code> extensions, the <code>runtime</code> commands, and the task commands. <code>doctor</code> and <code>guard</code> come next.</span></p>
      </div>
      <figure class="swatch">
        <figcaption>Terminal</figcaption>
<pre><code>$ solomonar init --runtime claude --runtime codex --yes
Initialized solomonar 0.3.3 in ~/ledger
  43 files created
  registry  refs/heads/workflow-state @ d769ccf

Next:
  1. First commit required before task worktrees
  2. Start a top-level session:
       Claude Code: /solomonar Explore the next useful flow.</code></pre>
      </figure>
    </section>
